            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 1)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "5627dc6e-c943-439e-ab4a-4531b7f24264"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Introduction to the Conflict</strong><br>\nThe conflict between Israelis and Palestinians has a long history that goes back many decades. Both groups claim the same land, which has led to many disputes. The situation is complex and is influenced by many political and religious factors.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Perspective of Israeli Teens</strong><br>\nIsraeli teenagers often grow up in an environment characterized by military presence and national security threats. Some see the conflict as a threat to their future and desire peace, while others may take a tougher stance towards the Palestinians. Their views are often shaped by personal experiences and upbringing from family and school.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Awareness</strong><br>\nIn Israel, there are educational programs that bring the conflict and its complexity closer to teenagers. These programs aim to create a better understanding and possibly a basis for future solutions. Education can help dismantle prejudices and develop a more nuanced view of the situation.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Perspective of Palestinian Teens</strong><br>\nOn the other hand, Palestinian teenagers often experience a different reality. They may suffer from poor living conditions and possibly have less access to education. Many see the conflict as a direct threat to their families and communities and desire a change in the current situation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Influence of Family and Community</strong><br>\nFamily and community play an essential role in Palestinian teenagers' perception of the conflict. Their views are often shaped by the experiences and stories of their elders. These personal stories can lead to a deeper understanding of the conflict or reinforce prejudices.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education System in Palestine</strong><br>\nIn Palestine, there are also educational efforts to inform teenagers about the conflict. However, these often face challenges, such as lack of resources or political influence. Nevertheless, educational programs can help develop a better understanding of the conflict's complexity.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
